    "cmd": "# FlashPro Express -> New Job Project (.job), or Libero SoC -> Programming Connectivity & Inspect Device",
    "note": "IGLOO2/SmartFusion2 expose a Microsemi PROGRAMMING TAP — no CoreSight DAP, no memory bus over JTAG.",
    "steps": [
      "Connect a FlashPro5/6 (or an FTDI in Microsemi mode) to the JTAG header.",
      "Inspect Device: read IDCODE + device/security status (FlashPro Express -> Inspect Device).",
      "If FlashLock / user pass-key / AES is NOT provisioned: eNVM + fabric bitstream readback may be possible.",
      "If security IS provisioned: readback is disabled by design -> identify + posture only, no dump."
    ]
  },

  // --- per-board adapter allowlist. Programming TAP, NO CPU -> tier ceiling is 'b' (+program). ---
  "adapters": [
    { "id": "flashpro4",  "name": "Microchip FlashPro4 (also FlashPro3)", "backend": "libero",  "driver": null,  "transports": ["jtag"],                  "usb_ids": [],            "tier": "b", "vendor_sw": true,  "note": "VID 0x1514 (Actel). Programming TAP only — no CPU/mem bus. IDCODE + boundary-scan + program/verify + eNVM/fabric readback IF FlashLock/pass-key/AES NOT provisioned; if provisioned, readback disabled by design." },
    { "id": "flashpro5-6", "name": "Microchip FlashPro5 / FlashPro6",     "backend": "libero",  "driver": null,  "transports": ["jtag"],                  "usb_ids": [],            "tier": "b", "vendor_sw": true,  "note": "Same Libero / FlashPro Express path. FlashPro5 is FTDI(FT4232H)-based -> a raw-FTDI OpenOCD route MIGHT exist (unverified)." },
